# package.json / package-lock.json used to be ignored here, from when this repo
# was purely static files and npm existed only for dev tooling. They are tracked
# now: mcp/ is a real Node service, so its dependencies and the `type: module`
# markers (js/package.json, mcp/package.json) have to travel with the repo or a
# fresh clone / cloud deploy fails on the first import. Note the bare pattern
# also matched EVERY nested package.json, not just the root one.

